1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,750
Jane: Hello, Jane Fairbanks speaking.

2
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:07,120
Frank: Oh, good morning. My name's Frank Pritchard

3
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:10,010
I've just retired and moved to Southoe.

4
00:00:10,010 --> 00:00:12,080
I'd like to become a volunteer

5
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:16,270
and I gather you co-ordinate voluntary work in the village.

6
00:00:16,270 --> 00:00:17,250
Jane: That's right.

7
00:00:17,250 --> 00:00:19,850
Frank: What sort of thing could I do?

8
00:00:19,850 --> 00:00:23,382
Jane: Well, we need help with the village library.

9
00:00:23,382 --> 00:00:28,091
We borrow books from the town library, and individuals also donate them.

10
00:00:28,091 --> 00:00:33,660
So, one thing you could do is get involved in collecting them

11
00:00:33,860 --> 00:00:35,940
if you've got a car, that is.

12
00:00:35,940 --> 00:00:38,100
Frank: Yes, that's no problem.

13
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:42,730
Jane: The times are pretty flexible so we can arrange it to suit you.

14
00:00:42,730 --> 00:00:47,360
Another thing is the records that we keep of the books we're given,

15
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:51,329
and those we borrow and need to return to the town library.

16
00:00:51,329 --> 00:00:56,620
It would be very useful to have another person to help keep them up to date.

17
00:00:56,620 --> 00:01:02,490
Frank: Right. I'm used to working on a computer - I presume they're computerised?

18
00:01:02,490 --> 00:01:03,810
Jane: Oh yes.

19
00:01:03,810 --> 00:01:07,820
Frank: Is the library purpose-built? I haven't noticed it

20
00:01:07,820 --> 00:01:09,260
when I've walked round the village.

21
00:01:09,260 --> 00:01:14,458
Jane: No, we simply have the use of a room in the village hall, the West Room.

22
00:01:14,458 --> 00:01:17,210
It's on the left as you go in.

23
00:01:17,210 --> 00:01:20,510
Frank: I must go and have a look inside the hall.

24
00:01:20,510 --> 00:01:22,680
Jane: Yes, it's a nice building.

25
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:26,640
Frank: Do you run a lunch club in the village for elderly people

26
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,000
I know a lot of places do.

27
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,810
Jane: Yes, we have a very successful club.

28
00:01:31,810 --> 00:01:35,860
Frank: I could help with transport, if that's of any use.

29
00:01:35,860 --> 00:01:40,128
Jane: Oh, definitely. People come to the club from neighbouring villages,

30
00:01:40,128 --> 00:01:43,620
and we're always in need of more drivers.

31
00:01:43,620 --> 00:01:48,906
Frank: And does the club have groups that focus on a particular hobby, too?

32
00:01:48,906 --> 00:01:54,570
I could get involved in one or two, particularly if there are any art groups.

33
00:01:54,570 --> 00:01:59,890
Jane: Excellent. I'll find out where we need help and get back to you.

34
00:01:59,890 --> 00:02:06,380
Frank: Fine. What about help for individual residents. Do you arrange that at all?

35
00:02:06,380 --> 00:02:11,498
Jane: Yes, we do it as a one-off. In fact, there's Mrs.

36
00:02:11,498 --> 00:02:15,560
Carroll. She needs a lift to the hospital next week

37
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:18,190
and we're struggling to find someone.

38
00:02:18,190 --> 00:02:19,860
Frank: When's her appointment?

39
00:02:19,860 --> 00:02:23,680
Jane: On Tuesday. It would take the whole morning.

40
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:25,010
Frank: I could do that.

41
00:02:25,010 --> 00:02:27,480
Jane: Oh, that would be great. Thank you

42
00:02:27,900 --> 00:02:32,721
And also, next week, we're arranging to have some work done to Mr.

43
00:02:32,721 --> 00:02:38,329
Selsbury's house before he moves, as he isn't healthy enough to do it himself.

44
00:02:38,329 --> 00:02:41,483
We've got some people to decorate his kitchen,

45
00:02:41,483 --> 00:02:46,390
but if you could do some weeding in his garden, that would be wonderful.

46
00:02:46,390 --> 00:02:52,530
Frank: OK. I'd enjoy that. And presumably the day and time are flexible.

47
00:02:52,530 --> 00:02:58,030
Jane: Oh yes. Just say when would suit you best, and we'll let Mr. Selsbury know.

48
00:02:58,030 --> 00:02:58,940
Frank: Good.

49
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:02,670
Jane: The Volunteers Group also organises monthly social events,

50
00:03:02,670 --> 00:03:07,310
which is a great way to meet other people, of course.

51
00:03:07,310 --> 00:03:08,150
Frank: Uhuh.

52
00:03:08,150 --> 00:03:13,849
Jane: So next month, on the 19th of October, we're holding a quiz -

53
00:03:13,849 --> 00:03:18,440
a couple of residents are great at planning unusual ones

54
00:03:18,440 --> 00:03:20,770
and we always fill the village hall.

55
00:03:20,770 --> 00:03:24,820
Frank: That sounds like fun. Can I do anything to help?

56
00:03:24,820 --> 00:03:27,500
Jane: Well, because of the number of people

57
00:03:28,040 --> 00:03:31,214
we need plenty of refreshments for halfway through.

58
00:03:31,214 --> 00:03:35,210
So, if you could provide any, we'd be grateful.

59
00:03:35,210 --> 00:03:39,800
Frank: I'm sure I could. I'll think about what to make, and let you know.

60
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:45,780
Jane: Thank you. Then on November the 18th, we're holding a dance

61
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:47,074
also in the village hall.

62
00:03:47,074 --> 00:03:51,924
We've booked a band that specialises in music of the 1930s -

63
00:03:51,924 --> 00:03:58,390
they've been before, and we've had a lot of requests to bring them back.

64
00:03:58,390 --> 00:04:03,030
Frank: I'm not really a dancer, but I'd like to do something to help.

65
00:04:03,030 --> 00:04:06,200
Jane: Well, we sell tickets in advance

66
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:09,716
and having an extra person to check them at the door,

67
00:04:09,716 --> 00:04:12,040
as people arrive, would be good

68
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:16,030
it can be quite a bottleneck if everyone arrives at once!

69
00:04:16,030 --> 00:04:18,400
Frank: OK, I'm happy with that.

70
00:04:18,400 --> 00:04:22,215
Jane: We're also arranging a New Year's Eve party.

71
00:04:22,215 --> 00:04:25,684
We're expecting that to be a really big event,

72
00:04:25,684 --> 00:04:30,540
so instead of the village hall, it'll be held in the Mountfort Hotel.

73
00:04:30,540 --> 00:04:31,620
Frank: The...?

74
00:04:31,620 --> 00:04:41,292
Jane: Mountfort. M-O-U-N-T-F-O-R-T Hotel. It isn't in Southoe itself, but it's only a couple of miles away.

75
00:04:41,292 --> 00:04:47,401
The hotel will be providing dinner and we've booked a band.

76
00:04:47,401 --> 00:04:55,400
The one thing we haven't got yet is a poster

77
00:04:55,840 --> 00:04:59,110
That isn't something you could do, by any chance, is it?

78
00:04:59,110 --> 00:05:04,280
Frank: Well actually, yes. Before I retired I was a graphic designer

79
00:05:04,400 --> 00:05:06,450
so that's right up my street.

80
00:05:06,450 --> 00:05:09,780
Jane: Oh perfect! I'll give you the details

81
00:05:09,780 --> 00:05:12,700
and then perhaps you could send me a draft...

82
00:05:12,700 --> 00:05:14,000
Frank: Of course.
